cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or findings, please cite as below."
title: "Calibration-statistic mismatch in AlphaGenome variant scoring"
authors:
  - family-names: "Amrutham"
    given-names: "Kavya"
    affiliation: "Barnard College, Columbia University"
    email: "ka3041@barnard.edu"
date-released: 2026-04-27
url: "https://github.com/kavya1a/regulatory-score-saturation"
abstract: >
  AlphaGenome's published quantile calibration is built on single-track
  summary statistics. When max-over-tracks aggregation is composed on top of
  these outputs, saturation collapses correlation against measured MPRA log
  fold change from rho = 0.123 to rho = 0.037 (Tewhey 2016, n = 3,246). We
  re-derive the quantile calibration on a max-over-tracks common-variant null
  (5,941 random gnomAD MAF>0.01 SNVs) and show the full underlying signal is
  recovered at rho = 0.123 (95% CI [0.088, 0.157], p = 2.5e-12). The
  saturation is an artifact of the calibration-statistic mismatch, not of
  the model.
keywords:
  - GWAS
  - regulatory genomics
  - variant scoring
  - MPRA
  - AlphaGenome
  - quantile calibration
  - matched-statistic calibration
  - fine-mapping
license: MIT
